From 3adf3650df24198aafded8b94402a3fcabbfc446 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FerrionOS <noreply@ferrionos.invalid>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 20:59:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] layout: Arrange each workspace freely or in columns (F4)

A workspace now has a mode, free or columns. In a free workspace every
window floats; only a fullscreen or maximized window sits in the
scrolling layout, and it returns to floating when it leaves that state.
A columns workspace is niri's own.

- The mode comes from `layout { workspace-mode "free" }`, globally or
  for an output, as the default for new workspaces: a config reload
  gives a changed default to the workspaces without windows and
  rearranges no window. The same option in a named workspace's own
  `layout` is that workspace's and follows a reload, unless the
  workspace was switched by hand.
- `toggle-workspace-mode` and `set-workspace-mode` switch the focused
  workspace and move every window across at its size. Going to columns
  lines the windows up from left to right, except the ones niri floats
  by itself; going back gives each window its last free place and size.
- A new window opens floating on a free workspace: the three callers
  of `compute_open_floating` in `xdg_shell.rs` ask the workspace.
- On a free workspace, the actions that would turn a fullscreen or
  maximized column back into a normal column are refused: consume and
  expel, column and window size changes, interactive resize, and moving
  a floating window to the columns.
- The IPC workspace record carries the mode. The default config makes
  new workspaces free and binds Mod+Shift+Space.

Checked: the new randomized-test operations and invariants failed
against a stub that only flipped the mode, and pass with this change,
also with RUN_SLOW_TESTS=1 and 20000 cases; 13 unit tests in
src/layout/tests/free.rs; `cargo test --all --exclude
niri-visual-tests` passes.
